+### (q) The S3 continuity flag is a CONSTANT FALSE: real defect, zero voided results, one MASKED break **[ADDED 2026-09-06 [i0cm]]**
+
+`8rugb`'s claim that the flag "taken at face value voids 100% of runs of any lane using this driver"
+is **REAL as a defect and REFUTED as a blast radius**, adjudicated at **$0** over the existing
+captures.
+
+**The flag has never once been true.** Across **151 driver records** in **9 capture roots**
+(`dialin`, `rebaseline`, `threeknob`, `161-presets`, `j0u`, `ytg`, `h7n`, `8rugb`, `otr-armb`),
+`session_continuity_ok` is `false` **151/151**. A field that is constant across every run of every
+arm carries **zero discriminating information**: it cannot have moved any comparison, and any lane
+that had gated on it would have had **0 valid runs and published nothing**. All 9 roots published.
+**No lane ever dropped, re-ran, or invalidated a run because of it** -- and the artifact was already
+documented, in `scenarios/s3/RESULTS.md`'s own "Honest caveats" (all 71 copies), in
+`20260901-rebaseline/REPORT.md`, in `20260901-threeknob/LEG-B-REPORT.md`, and worked around
+independently twice (`remeasure_s3.sh`'s `resume_sid_consistent`; `8rugb`'s `summarize_run.py`).
+
+**Re-run with the corrected check, 148/151 are continuous.** The 3 that are not:
+`rebaseline/val-rb-oai-sol-xhigh-s3-{01,02}` (last turn TIMEOUT -- already excluded by
+`turns_done != 5`), and **one genuine break nobody saw**:
+**`threeknob/runs/val-tk-sol-xhigh-s3-02` ran turns 1-4 in `1f19b7ad...` and turn 5 in
+`8839b22c...`** -- a session that appears **nowhere in the capture** -- while the root session file
+carries **4** `prompt:complete`, not 5. It scored **90/100, pass=True**, and was counted.
+
+**That is the actual cost of this defect, and it is the inverse of the claim.** The flag did not void
+valid runs; it **cried wolf on all 151, so one real break was indistinguishable from the noise.** A
+constant alarm is not a conservative alarm.
+
+**Every affected conclusion STANDS. Nothing is VOID; nothing needs a re-run.**
+
+| conclusion | verdict | why |
+|---|---|---|
+| (c) three-knob frontier [threeknob, 64 S3 runs] | **STANDS** | 63/64 continuous. Dropping the one broken run leaves the `sol-xhigh` S3 median at **90 either way** (100/90/80 -> 100/80); no headline claim rests on `sol-xhigh` S3 (the sol counter-example in (c) is stated on S1). Pass count moves 2/3 -> 1/2, stated for honesty. |
