+**The rule this buys:** a validity flag that is constant across the whole corpus is not evidence of
+validity **or** of invalidity -- it is an uncalibrated instrument, and it must be checked against a
+value whose answer is already known before any run is judged by it. Same family as S2a's vacuous
+Gate 3 and the unsatisfiable condition in (p): **an instrument that cannot come out both ways has
